{"step_index":83,"source":"SYSTEM","type":"CHECKPOINT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-01T18:19:45Z","content":"{{ CHECKPOINT 1 }}\n **The earlier parts of this conversation have been truncated due to its long length. The following content summarizes the truncated context so that you may continue your work. **\n\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. use this charaker for blender and make one 2d animation of walking lafing and some assets fist waht you are going to do tell me beucse i want min 20 sec video like animation like so create a whole idea of it and the figure i gave you of stickman it should be the main character so do it with mulitple expressions \n2. i am not goint to do anything you have to do it here so do i all by understing the plan what changes reduqied\n\n# Previous Session Summary:\n### 1. Outstanding User Requests\n- **Request:** \"use this charaker for blender and make one 2d animation of walking lafing and some assets fist waht you are going to do tell me beucse i want min 20 sec video like animation like so create a whole idea of it and the figure i gave you of stickman it should be the main character so do it with mulitple expressions\" -> \"i am not goint to do anything you have to do it here so do i all by understing the plan what changes reduqied\"\n- **Current Phase:** IMPLEMENTATION\n- **Status:** The storyboard was approved. Fully automated scripts were written to handle image processing and Blender animation without user intervention. The Blender render is currently running in the background.\n\n### 2. User Knowledge\n- **Initial Request:** The user provided an uploaded image of a stickman (`media_1788285703286.png`) and explicitly requested a minimum 20-second 2D animation created in Blender featuring the character walking and laughing with multiple expressions.\n- **Workflow Constraints:** When presented with manual tracing steps in Blender, the user strictly refused manual work: \"i am not goint to do anything you have to do it here so do i all by understing the plan what changes reduqied\". Everything must be fully automated.\n\n### 3. Work Accomplished\n- **Planning:** Created and got user approval for the 20-second storyboard (`blender_animation_plan.md`).\n- **Asset Generation:** Wrote and executed `remove_bg.py` using OpenCV to extract the stickman from its yellow background and generate a second state with a procedurally drawn laughing mouth. (Assets saved as `stickman_bored.png` and `stickman_laugh.png`).\n- **Animation Automation:** Wrote `animate_stickman_auto.py` to run headless in Blender. It automatically sets up an Orthographic camera, loads the images as materials onto planes, rigs the planes to a parent Empty, and inserts keyframes for a 20-second waddle walk cycle and a faster laughing cycle while swapping the visibility of the expression planes.\n- **Video Compilation:** Wrote `compile_video.py` using OpenCV to stitch the resulting PNG frame sequence into a final MP4 video.\n\n### 4. Model Knowledge\n- **Blender Headless Quirks & Constraints:**\n  - `active_material_index` is NOT animatable. To swap expressions, you must use two separate overlapping planes and toggle their `hide_render` and `hide_viewport` keyframes.\n  - Materials API changed in Blender 4.2+ (EEVEE Next). Attributes like `shadow_method` and `blend_method` on `Material` throw `AttributeError`. EEVEE Next handles transparency via node connections alone.\n  - Headless Blender on this Windows machine failed to recognize the `FFMPEG` file format enum, crashing the render. The pipeline was shifted to render a PNG sequence first, followed by OpenCV video compilation.\n  - `BLENDER_EEVEE_NEXT` took ~3 seconds per frame for simple unlit planes. The render engine in `animate_stickman_auto.py` was switched to `BLENDER_WORKBENCH` with `FLAT` lighting and `TEXTURE` color_type, which renders near-instantly.\n- **Executable Location:** Blender 5